{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Sport",
  "theme": "sportdash",
  "_about": "After BMW's Live Cockpit Sport view (photos of the X3's own cluster, measured on a warped overlay), generated by design/gen_sport.py (edit that and regenerate): blue speed (0..200 mph) and red rev (0..7000 rpm, the M40i's own scale) brackets, each a bright outer line, a filling band, a dark gap and an inner line, a big speed in the middle with the gear and the drive mode under it, fuel and oil temperature bars, boost and coolant on the blue / red bar. The middle is black; while the Waze map shows inside the theme ('Show Waze map inside the theme', 'mapUp') it is cut see-through over the map (content z 0, under this shader at z 1), inset 'holeInset' px with 'holeRadius' corners, 16 px clear of the top and bottom lines, and a fuel line and the oil temperature stand in for the bars. Everything that isn't text is one shader (sdash), which ends at y 660 so BMW's own bottom strip (range, clock, mode, outside temperature) shows under it; the theme repeats none of those. The brackets and the gear keep clear of the black box BMW draws at x 1406..1597, y 342..419, and of the hood over the top corners. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header.",
